    - Automatic checkout to main/master for safety
    - Detailed logging of deleted branches and timestamps
    - Prevents accidental deletion of active development branches
    
    Usage:
      # Preview stale branches (dry-run)
      bash scripts/cleanup-stale-branches.sh --dry-run
    
      # Delete branches merged >30 days ago (default)
      bash scripts/cleanup-stale-branches.sh
    
      # Delete branches merged >60 days ago
      bash scripts/cleanup-stale-branches.sh --days 60
    
    Features:
      - Safe: Requires explicit confirmation (no auto-deletion)
      - Smart: Protects main/master branches
      - Configurable: Adjust --days threshold per use case
      - Reversible: Merged branches recoverable from git reflog
    
    Governance Benefits:
      - Keeps repository clean and maintainable
      - Reduces branch list clutter
      - Enforces cleanup discipline
      - Improves CI/CD performance (fewer branch checks)
    
    Recommended Setup:
      - Run quarterly with --days 60 for stable branches
      - Run monthly with --days 30 for feature cleanup
      - Add to CI pipeline for automated maintenance
    
